spec workflow    # Spec request: 3tched control plane + ghostbridge\n  mesh identity\n  Produce a full Kiro spec package:\n  1) requirements.md — EARS-style numbered requirements\n  (REQ-*), acceptance criteria, explicit non-goals\n  2) design.md — architecture, sequence flows, trust\n  boundaries, failure modes\n  3) tasks.md — implementation tasks each linked back to\n  REQ-* IDs (and design sections)\n  Do not implement code yet. Spec only. Prefer concrete,\n  testable requirements over prose.\n  ## Product naming / planes\n  - ghostbridge = mesh (WireGuard / NetMaker subscriber\n  fabric)\n  - 3tched = control plane\n  - Domains involved: 3tched.com, ghostbridge.tech (and\n  related owned names)\n  - Existing ops context (constraints, not invent new\n  platform):\n    - Single public VPS IP (e.g. 188.68.58.237)\n    - Open vSwitch + cookied OpenFlow managed flows\n  (safe attach; no delete-all)\n    - NetMaker for WG identity; all subscribers get WG\n  identity\n    - xray REALITY on public :443 for hostile-underlay\n  camouflage\n    - op-grpc-bridge on mesh (e.g. 10.0.0.2:8090)\n    - mail CT (postfix/dovecot) for real mail\n    - Cloudflare authoritative DNS + Email Routing\n  available\n    - Incus containers; Artix/runit host style is fine\n  to assume\n  ## Locked intent (must appear as requirements)\n  ### Access model\n  - After subscribe/join, dashboard, control plane,\n  gRPC, api, broker, qdrant, assistant are PRIVATE on\n  mesh only — not public browser TLS on VPS :443.\n  - Anonymous internet users must not have a happy path\n  to private control-plane services.\n  - Public Cloudflare surface is ONLY marketing site +\n  subscribe/registration UI (orange-proxied).\n  - No Cloudflare Tunnel / Workers TCP / durable data\n  stream / public REST|gRPC registration API into the\n  control plane as the primary path.\n  ### Registration / control channel\n  - Cloudflare → control plane communication for\n  registration MUST be email-triggered, NOT live data\n  streams.\n  - End user must NOT know about / see the\n  CF→control-plane email hop (opaque infrastructure).\n  - Async latency (seconds–minutes) is ACCEPTABLE;\n  registration is low volume.\n  - On subscribe submit: emit structured registration\n  mail/event toward control-plane ingest address.\n  - Control plane mail consumer parses trigger →\n  provisions NetMaker enrollment / WG grant / join\n  instructions.\n  - End-user UX may be “thanks, check email for join\n  steps” (or equivalent); never expose control-plane\n  URLs as the registration transport.\n  ### Mail (half-and-half) — critical\n  - Cloudflare Email Routing owns public inbound MX and\n  FORWARDS into the self-hosted mail CT.\n  - Mail CT is the real mailbox (IMAP) AND registered\n  outbound SMTP.\n  - Users/operators MUST be able to reply/send as\n  @3tched.com and @ghostbridge.tech from the mail CT.\n  - Gmail MUST NOT be a sender/From identity for those\n  domains (no Gmail Send-mail-as; no Gmail in SPF as\n  sender for branded From).\n  - Multi-domain demux: CF routing rules and/or mail CT\n  recipient/domain maps.\n  - Machine addresses (e.g. register@ / ingest@) land on\n  mail CT and trigger control-plane provision.\n  - Mail TLS/certs on mail ports 465/587/993 (ACME).\n  Mail is NOT terminated on REALITY :443.\n  - Align SPF/DKIM/DMARC so mail CT is sole outbound for\n  branded send.\n  ### Mesh / routing\n  - Known mesh services demux by IP:port via OpenFlow\n  (managed cookied flows / safe controller attach) — NOT\n  multi-domain public SNI demux for private names.\n  - gRPC-web UI is mesh-private, linked from private\n  dashboard, targeting op-grpc-bridge.\n  ### REALITY\n  - REALITY remains hostile-underlay camouflage ONLY.\n  - Single innocuous decoy serverName; owned service\n  names must NOT be in REALITY serverNames for “browser\n  HTTPS”.\n  - Authorized path: tunnel → mesh → OpenFlow →\n  services.\n  ### Explicit non-goals (must list)\n  - nginx/haproxy SNI front splitting dashboard vs\n  REALITY on public :443\n  - Public wildcard browser certs for private\n  dashboard/API names on VPS edge\n  - CF data streams / live tunnels into control plane\n  for subscribe\n  - Using Gmail as branded From for 3tched.com /\n  ghostbridge.*\n  - Putting private service names into REALITY\n  serverNames to fix browser certs\n  ## Required spec outputs\n  ### requirements.md\n  Group by: Public surface, Email control channel, Mail\n  hosting, Mesh privacy, OpenFlow routing, REALITY\n  camouflage, Identity/enrollment, Observability/ops,\n  Security/trust, Verification.\n  Each REQ must have: statement, rationale (short),\n  acceptance criteria (bullet, testable).\n  Include negative requirements (MUST NOT).\n  ### design.md\n  Include:\n  - Trust-boundary diagram (mermaid)\n  - Subscribe sequence: browser → CF form → email → mail\n  CT → CP → NetMaker/WG → mesh access\n  - Mail half-and-half inbound/outbound flows\n  - What is public vs mesh vs camouflage\n  - Failure modes: mail delay/loss, CF forward failure,\n  enrollment token expiry, REALITY misuse\n  - How OpenFlow demux fits without SNI front\n  - Rollback / safety notes for OVS (never delete-all;\n  cookied managed flows)\n  ### tasks.md\n  Ordered implementation tasks with:\n  - Task ID\n  - Description\n  - Linked REQ-* IDs\n  - Dependencies\n  - Definition of done / verification steps\n  Cover at least: CF DNS/proxy surface, CF Email Routing\n  rules, mail CT ACME+SPF/DKIM/DMARC+send/reply, email\n  ingest→provision pipeline, NetMaker enrollment grant,\n  mesh-only service binding, OpenFlow flows, REALITY\n  serverNames trim, private gRPC UI, end-to-end\n  verification checklist.\n  ## Quality bar\n  - No TBDs for locked decisions above; if something is\n  truly unknown, mark ASSUMPTION with a default and\n  impact.\n  - Prefer small verifiable tasks over mega-tasks.\n  - Use consistent IDs so requirements ↔ tasks are\n  traceable.\n\n  ────────────────────────────────────────\n\n  When Kiro returns the requirements + tasks spec, paste\n  the link (or drop the files here) and we can fold it\n  into the plan / execute from that.
/model
