# Spec revision request:\n  3tched-ghostbridge-control-plane\n  Update requirements.md, design.md, and tasks.md in\n  place. Do not implement code.\n  Keep what is already correct (CF orange surface, no CF\n  tunnels, REALITY single decoy, no SNI front on :443,\n  OpenFlow cookied IP:port, mail half-and-half no Gmail,\n  mesh binds). Fix the contradictions below.\n  ## Locked intent (source of truth — override the draft\n  where it conflicts)\n  - ghostbridge = mesh; 3tched = control plane\n  - All subscribers get WireGuard identity via NetMaker\n  - After join: dashboard / CP / gRPC / api / broker /\n  qdrant / assistant are mesh-only\n  - Public CF = marketing + subscribe UI only; no CF\n  data streams into CP\n  - CF → control plane = email trigger only (opaque\n  infrastructure; end user must not see that hop)\n  - Async seconds–minutes is OK for registration\n  - End-user UX MAY be “thanks, check your email for\n  join steps”\n  - Mail half-and-half: CF Email Routing inbound MX →\n  mail CT; ONLY mail CT sends/replies as @3tched.com /\n  @ghostbridge.* — NOT Gmail\n  - REALITY = optional hostile-underlay camouflage only\n  (single decoy SNI)\n  - OpenFlow demux by IP:port for known mesh services\n  - gRPC-web UI is mesh-private, linked from private\n  dashboard → op-grpc-bridge 10.0.0.2:8090\n  ---\n  ## MUST FIX (blocking)\n  ### 1) REQ-BACKEND-002 is wrong — rewrite\n  Current draft says user must NOT see “check your\n  email” and latency should feel like a normal page\n  load.\n  Correct:\n  - Opaque = the CF→control-plane email hop (no\n  control-plane URLs, no “talking to backend” UI).\n  - User-facing “check your email for join steps” is\n  ALLOWED and preferred.\n  - Latency is async (seconds–minutes), not a\n  synchronous page-load illusion.\n  ### 2) Delete ASSUMPTION-001 (CF return path / Workers\n  polling)\n  Do NOT invent CF Workers polling or live page-update\n  return paths from the control plane.\n  Correct completion path:\n  1. CF form emits structured registration mail → ingest\n  address\n  2. CF Email Routing forwards → mail CT\n  3. CP mail consumer parses → provisions NetMaker/WG\n  enrollment\n  4. mail CT sends join instructions TO THE SUBSCRIBER’S\n  EMAIL (outbound SMTP as @3tched.com / @ghostbridge.*)\n  5. Subscriber joins WG → mesh access\n  No CF live return channel.\n  ### 3) REALITY is NOT the primary subscriber path\n  REQ-REALITY-004, trust diagrams, mesh verification,\n  and TASK-021 currently treat “xray client + REALITY\n  tunnel” as the authorized path for everyone.\n  Correct:\n  - Primary identity/access = NetMaker WireGuard mesh\n  - REALITY = optional hostile-underlay camouflage path\n  only\n  - Do not require every subscriber to use an\n  xray/REALITY client\n  - Update design trust diagram + verification\n  accordingly (WG join success is the main E2E; REALITY\n  tunnel is a separate optional check)\n  ### 4) Clarify mail certs vs “no owned certs on VPS\n  edge”\n  REQ-SNI-003 / design rule “owned domain TLS certs do\n  not exist on VPS public edge” conflicts with mail.*.\n  Correct:\n  - Forbidden: browser-trusted certs for private web\n  names on public :443\n  - Allowed/required: ACME certs for mail.3tched.com /\n  mail.ghostbridge.tech on :465/:587/:993\n  ### 5) Fix broken REQ link\n  TASK-002 links REQ-SEC-001 which does not exist. Add a\n  Security/trust REQ section or retarget the link.\n  ---\n  ## MUST ADD (missing from locked intent)\n  ### Requirements — add sections/REQs for:\n  - **Identity/enrollment:** subscribe submit →\n  structured ingest mail; CP consumer; NetMaker node/WG\n  grant; outbound join mail from mail CT; no public\n  REST/gRPC registration API on VPS edge\n  - **Mail demux:** CF routing rules and/or CT maps for\n  multi-domain; human mailboxes vs machine addresses\n  (register@ / ingest@)\n  - **Human send/reply:** operators can IMAP + SMTP\n  submit and reply as branded From (not just SPF theory)\n  - **Private gRPC UI:** mesh-only gRPC-web UI linked\n  from private dashboard to 10.0.0.2:8090\n  - **Negative:** Gmail must not be a CF Email Routing\n  destination for branded domains (not only “not in\n  SPF”)\n  ### Design — add:\n  - Subscribe sequence mermaid: browser → CF form →\n  email → CF Routing → mail CT → CP → NetMaker → join\n  mail to user → WG → mesh → OpenFlow → services\n  - Explicit note: REALITY optional; WG primary\n  - Failure modes already partial — add: mail\n  delay/loss, enrollment token expiry, ingest parse\n  failure, join-mail delivery failure\n  - Keep OVS safety (never unfiltered del-flows; cookied\n  managed flows; fail-mode standalone)\n  ### Tasks — add ordered tasks (with REQ links, deps,\n  DoD):\n  - CF subscribe form emits structured registration\n  email to ingest address (no CP URL)\n  - CF Email Routing rules for human + ingest/register\n  addresses → mail CT (both domains)\n  - Mail ingest consumer → NetMaker enrollment grant\n  - Outbound join-instructions email from mail CT\n  - Private gRPC-web UI on mesh + dashboard link\n  - E2E verify: subscribe → ingest mail → provision →\n  user receives join mail → WG join → mesh\n  dashboard/gRPC work; user never hits CP URL; REALITY\n  optional check separate\n  ---\n  ## KEEP / DO NOT REGRESS\n  - No nginx/haproxy SNI front on public :443\n  - No public wildcard browser certs for private\n  dashboard/API on VPS :443\n  - No CF Tunnel / Workers TCP / live streams into CP\n  for subscribe\n  - No Gmail Send-mail-as / Gmail in SPF for branded\n  From\n  - No owned names in REALITY serverNames\n  - OpenFlow cookie + no bulk delete safety\n  ## Output\n  Revise all three files. Bump version to 1.1. Summarize\n  changes at top of each file under “Revision 1.1”.\n\n  Highest-impact mistakes in the draft: it forbids\n  “check your email,” invents a CF return path, and\n  makes REALITY mandatory instead of optional\n  camouflage.
# Spec revision 1.2: 3tched-ghostbridge-control-plane\n  1.1 fixed the prior blockers. Apply these remaining\n  fixes in requirements.md, design.md, tasks.md. Spec\n  only.\n  ## MUST FIX\n  ### A) Soften REQ-CF-001 overclaim\n  “Users cannot discover VPS IP from normal web\n  interaction” is false once mail.*/SPF exist.\n  Rewrite acceptance to: public *web* hostnames resolve\n  to CF; mail.* and SPF MAY publish VPS IP by design.\n  ### B) Align REQ-SEC-001 with REQ-CF-002\n  SEC-001 currently bans tunnels only as “primary” path.\n  Make it absolute for control-plane ingress: no CF\n  Tunnel / Workers TCP / live streams into CP at all\n  (same bar as CF-002). Email trigger remains the only\n  CF→CP control channel.\n  ### C) Make TASK-004 / form→email mechanism concrete\n  (no VPS HTTP)\n  “CF Pages Function or Workers send email” needs an\n  explicit allowed mechanism:\n  - MUST emit structured mail into CF Email Routing /\n  Email Workers send path toward ingest@\n  - MUST NOT HTTP/gRPC/WebSocket to VPS or open CF\n  Tunnel\n  Add ASSUMPTION: CF Email Workers (or equivalent\n  CF-native outbound mail) is available; if not,\n  document the chosen CF-side mail emit method without\n  VPS callback.\n  ### D) Cross-spec topology with\n  netmaker-xray-identity-handoff (blocking drift)\n  Handoff hard-bounds: human WG terminates ONLY at\n  Oracle decoy; no host `wg-lan`; NetMaker is transport,\n  not identity authority.\n  This CP spec currently reads as: enroll NetMaker node\n  on mesh; subscriber WG directly to NetMaker as\n  PRIMARY.\n  Add an “Adjacent specs / identity topology” section\n  that locks ONE of these (choose and write as decided,\n  do not leave optional):\n  **Chosen default (align both specs):**\n  - Human identity WG terminates at Oracle decoy (per\n  handoff).\n  - NetMaker = single decoy→host transport (+ mesh\n  addressing), NOT a second human identity plane.\n  - Join email provisions decoy/NetMaker enrollment\n  consistent with that path (not host WG interface).\n  - Application auth after join is assertion-validated\n  at op-grpc-bridge (handoff); this CP owns email enroll\n  + mail + public surface + REALITY camouflage ops\n  only.\n  - Cross-link\n  `.kiro/specs/netmaker-xray-identity-handoff/`.\n  - Explicit non-goal here: implementing Oracle\n  assertion crypto (owned by handoff).\n  Update REQ-MESH-003 / REQ-ID-003 / design trust\n  diagram / TASK-018 language so “WG primary” does not\n  mean “WG terminates on VPS host”.\n  ### E) Add missing links\n  - TASK-004 also links REQ-ID-005\n  - Design verification E2E already good; add one line\n  that HumanPrincipal/assertion path is verified under\n  handoff mission, not this task list\n  ## KEEP\n  All 1.1 decisions (check-email UX, no CF return path,\n  REALITY optional, mail half-and-half no Gmail,\n  OpenFlow cookie safety, mesh-private gRPC UI).\n  Bump to Version 1.2; add Revision 1.2 notes at top of\n  each file.
